:"gederah","g":"folds","fb":[],"v":[4734,4742,4754,7842,15365,20129,21563,22728,22810]},"H1425":{"l":"גָּדִי","x":"Gâdîy","d":"a Gadite (collectively) or descendants of Gad","p":"gaw-dee'","t":"gadi","g":"Gadite[s]","fb":[],"v":[4830,4987,4991,5047,5687,5863,6136,6162,6427,8689,9826,10446,10454,10728,10757,11109]},"H1474":{"l":"גּוֹלָן","x":"Gôwlân","d":"Golan, a place east of the Jordan","p":"go-lawn'","t":"golan","g":"Golan","fb":[["golan","Golan","","One of the three cities of refuge east of the Jordan, in Bashan, where someone who had killed by accident could run from revenge. It went to the Gershonite Levites and later gave its name to the region, which is why there are Golan Heights today. The exact site is not known.","place",4]],"v":[5047,6380,6408,10525]},"H1438":{"l":"גָּדַע","x":"gâdaʻ","d":"to fell a tree; generally, to destroy anything","p":"gaw-dah'","t":"gada","g":"he cut down","fb":[],"v":[5116,5243,7108,7271,11478,11855,11937,11940,15080,15714,17838,17882,17939,18076,18562,20104,20188,20334,20568,22408,23037,23041]},"H1412":{"l":"גֻּדְגֹּדָה","x":"Gudgôdâh","d":"Gudgodah, a place in the Desert","p":"gud-go'-daw","t":"gudgodah","g":"(the)","fb":[["gudgodah","Gudgodah","Hor-haggidgad","A wilderness stop in Deuteronomy 10:7, just after Moserah where Aaron died. Numbers 33 calls it Hor-haggidgad, and its place in Sinai has not been found.","place",1]],"v":[5193,5193]},"H1413":{"l":"גָּדַד","x":"gâdad","d":"to crowd; also to gash (as if by pressing into)","p":"gaw-dad'","t":"gadad","g":"they cut themselves","fb":[],"v":[5291,9369,15451,19064,19341,19961,20077,22633]},"H1488":{"l":"גֵּז","x":"gêz","d":"a fleece (as shorn); also mown grass","p":"gaze","t":"gez","g":"the mowings","fb":[],"v":[5388,13607,15005,22464]},"H1434":{"l":"גְּדִל","x":"gᵉdil","d":"thread, i.e. a tassel or festoon","p":"ghed-eel'","t":"gedil","g":"wreaths","fb":[],"v":[5482,8951]},"H1415":{"l":"גָּדָה","x":"gâdâh","d":"a border of a river (as cut into by the stream)","p":"gaw-daw'","t":"gadah","g":"banks","fb":[],"v":[5908,5928,10735,17813]},"H1445":{"l":"גֶּדֶר","x":"Geder","d":"Geder, a place in Palestine","p":"gheh'-der","t":"geder","g":"of Geder","fb":[["geder","Geder","Gedor","Joshua beat its king. Whether it is the same place as Gedor or Gederah is possible, not certain.","place",1]],"v":[6143]},"H1449":{"l":"גְּדֵרָה","x":"Gᵉdêrâh","d":"(with the article) Gederah, a place in Palestine","p":"ghed-ay-raw'","t":"gederah","g":"Gederah","fb":[["gederah","Gederah","","It sat in the Shephelah, Judah's lowland, and Chronicles names potters of Judah's line who lived there and worked for the king.","place",2]],"v":[6238,10408]},"H1453":{"l":"גְּדֵרֹתַיִם","x":"Gᵉdêrôthayim","d":"Gederothajim, a place in Palestine","p":"ghed-ay-ro-thah'-yim","t":"gederothayim","g":"Gederothaim","fb":[["gederothaim","Gederothaim","","Listed right after Gederah in Joshua 15:36. The ending can mean two, so some read it as the two Gederahs rather than a town of its own, and if it was separate nobody has found where.","place",1]],"v":[6238]},"H1450":{"l":"גְּדֵרוֹת","x":"Gᵉdêrôwth","d":"Gederoth, a place in Palestine","p":"ghed-ay-rohth'","t":"gederoth","g":"Gederoth","fb":[["gederoth","Gederoth","","The Philistines took it in the reign of Ahaz, while Judah was worn down by war with Israel and Syria. It was a Shephelah town, and the name means sheepfolds.","place",2]],"v":[6243,11782]},"H1446":{"l":"גְדֹר","x":"Gᵉdôr","d":"Gedor, a place in Palestine; also the name of three Israelites","p":"ghed-ore'","t":"gedor","g":"Gedor","fb":[["gedor","Gedor","","A town in the hill country of Judah between Jerusalem and Hebron, whose founders Chronicles traces through Hur and Ephrathah. The same name belongs to another place and to a man in Saul's family.","place",4],["gedor-2","Gedor","Man living at the time of United Monarchy","1 Chronicles names him twice, and he is a man from the united kingdom.","person",2],["gedor-3","Gedor","","1 Chronicles names him once, and nothing else is recorded.","place",1]],"v":[6260,10389,10403,10424,10606,10652,10727]},"H1405":{"l":"גִּבְּתוֹן","x":"Gibbᵉthôwn","d":"Gibbethon, a place in Palestine","p":"ghib-beth-one'","t":"gibbethon","g":"Gibbethon","fb":[["gibbethon","Gibbethon","","In Dan's territory and assigned to the Kohath family, but the Philistines held it most of the time. Nadab was besieging it when his officer Baasha killed him and took the throne. A generation later Elah went the same way while his army was at the same city again.","place",5]],"v":[6365,6404,9276,9276,9298,9300]},"H1439":{"l":"גִּדְעוֹן","x":"Gidʻôwn","d":"Gidon, an Israelite","p":"ghid-ohn'","t":"gidon","g":"Gideon","fb":[["gideon","Gideon","Judge living before Israel's Monarchy","An angel found him threshing wheat in a winepress, hiding it from the Midianites, and called him a mighty man of valour. Gideon asked for the fleece to be wet and then dry before he believed it. God cut his army from thirty-two thousand to three hundred, and they took the Midianite camp at night with torches, trumpets and empty jars.","person",37]],"v":[6665,6667,6673,6676,6676,6678,6681,6683,6688,6690,6693,6695,6696,6698,6699,6701,6707,6708,6709,6712,6713,6714,6718,6719,6723,6726,6730,6732,6740,6741,6742,6743,6746,6746,6747,6749,6751,6752,6754]},"H1492":{"l":"גָּזַּה","x":"gâzzah","d":"a fleece","p":"gaz-zaw'","t":"gazzah","g":"fleece","fb":[],"v":[6691,6691,6692,6692,6693,6693,6694]},"H1440":{"l":"גִּדְעֹם","x":"Gidʻôm","d":"Gidom, a place in Palestine","p":"ghid-ohm'","t":"gidom","g":"Gidom","fb":[["gidom","Gidom","","Judges 20:45 names it once, as a point on the road where the retreating Benjamite army was cut down. It lay somewhere between Gibeah and the rock of Rimmon, and nobody knows exactly where.","place",1]],"v":[7099]},"H1420":{"l":"גְּדוּלָה","x":"gᵉdûwlâh","d":"greatness; (concretely) mighty acts","p":"ghed-oo-law'","t":"gedulah","g":"greatness","fb":[],"v":[8201,8203,10882,10882,10884,11175,12705,12795,12867,14996,16322,16325]},"H1417":{"l":"גְּדוּד","x":"gᵉdûwd","d":"a furrow (as cut)","p":"ghed-ood'","t":"gedud","g":"a marauding band","fb":[],"v":[8632,14146,14869]},"H1458":{"l":"גַּו","x":"gav","d":"the back","p":"gav","t":"gav","g":"back","fb":[],"v":[9227,12536,21041]},"H1457":{"l":"גָּהַר","x":"gâhar","d":"to prostrate oneself","p":"gaw-har'","t":"gahar","g":"he bent down","fb":[],"v":[9383,9637,9638]},"H1483":{"l":"גּוּר","x":"Gûwr","d":"Gur, a place in Palestine","p":"goor","t":"gur","g":"of Gur","fb":[["gur","Gur","","Jehu's servants caught King Ahaziah of Judah on the ascent of Gur, near Ibleam, as he ran, and wounded him fatally.","place",1]],"v":[9783]},"H1443":{"l":"גָּדַר","x":"gâdar","d":"to wall in or around","p":"gaw-dar'","t":"gadar","g":"he has walled up","fb":[],"v":[9862,10151,13304,18797,20360,20362,20712,21005,22110,22505]},"H1424":{"l":"גָּדִי","x":"Gâdîy","d":"Gadi, an Israelite","p":"gaw-dee'","t":"gadi","g":"of Gadi","fb":[["gadi","Gadi","Man living at the time of Divided Monarchy","Only ever named as the father of Menahem, who killed Shallum, took the throne of Israel and ruled brutally.","person",2]],"v":[9939,9942]},"H1470":{"l":"גּוֹזָן","x":"Gôwzân","d":"Gozan, a province of Assyria","p":"go-zawn'","t":"gozan","g":"of Gozan","fb":[["gozan","Gozan","","When Assyria took the northern kingdom, it resettled Israelite captives in this region of northern Mesopotamia.","place",5]],"v":[9989,10035,10073,10454,18363]},"H1473":{"l":"גּוֹלָה","x":"gôwlâh","d":"exile; concretely and collectively exiles","p":"go-law'","t":"golah","g":"exile[s]","fb":[],"v":[10217,10218,10450,12027,12028,12111,12170,12171,12172,12236,12241,12258,12259,12260,12268,12426,12729,19623,19635,19638,19650,19654,19665,20063,20086,20090,20129,20464,20512,20516,20678,20679,20682,20683,20683,20686,20690,21085,22378,22721,22956,23069]},"H1436":{"l":"גְּדַּלְיָה","x":"Gᵉdalyâh","d":"Gedaljah, the name of five Israelites","p":"ghed-al-yaw'","t":"gedalyah","g":"Gedaliah","fb":[["gedaliah","Gedaliah","Governor living at the time of Divided Monarchy","After Jerusalem fell, Babylon made him governor of Judah over the poor left in the land, and he told them to settle down and submit. Ishmael, of the royal line, murdered him within months, and the rest fled to Egypt in spite of Jeremiah telling them not to go.","person",26],["gedaliah-2","Gedaliah","Levite living at the time of United Monarchy","1 Chronicles names him twice, and he is a Levite from the united kingdom.","person",2],["gedaliah-4","Gedaliah","Man living at the time of Divided Monarchy","A man from the divided-kingdom years, and Jeremiah is the only book that names him.","person",1],["gedaliah-5","Gedaliah","Man living at the time of Divided Monarchy","A man from the divided-kingdom years. Zephaniah names him once.","person",1],["gedaliah-3","Gedaliah","Man living at the time of Exile and Return","One of 5 men called Gedaliah. This one is a man from the exile and the return, named once in Ezra.","person",1]],"v":[10244,10245,10245,10246,10247,11049,11055,12270,19895,19936,19945,19946,19947,19948,19949,19951,19952,19953,19954,19955,19956,19957,19958,19959,19960,19962,19965,19966,19972,19974,20002,22787]},"H1495":{"l":"גָּזֵז","x":"Gâzêz","d":"Gazez, the name of two Israelites","p":"gaw-zaze'","t":"gazez","g":"Gazez","fb":[["gazez","Gazez","","Two men in one verse. One is Caleb's son by his concubine Ephah, the other is a son of Haran, Ephah's son, and so the first one's nephew. Some think the second is a scribe repeating himself, but the text as it stands has two.","person",1]],"v":[10352,10352]},"H1463":{"l":"גּוֹג","x":"Gôwg","d":"Gog, the name of an Israelite, also of some northern nation","p":"gohg","t":"gog","g":"Gog","fb":[["gog","Gog","","Ezekiel's enemy from the land of Magog, leading a huge coalition against restored Israel, and God himself destroys him. Revelation uses the name again for the nations gathered in a last rebellion.","place",8],["gog-2","Gog","Man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness","1 Chronicles names him once, and he is a man from the wilderness years.","person",1]],"v":[10432,21426,21427,21438,21440,21442,21448,21448,21458,21458]},"H1480":{"l":"גּוּפָה","x":"gûwphâh","d":"a corpse (as closed to sense)","p":"goo-faw'","t":"guphah","g":"the corpse","fb":[],"v":[10671,10671]},"H1493":{"l":"גִּזוֹנִי","x":"Gizôwnîy","d":"a Gizonite or inhabitant of Gizoh","p":"ghee-zo-nee'","t":"gizoni","g":"Gizonite","fb":[["gizonite","Gizonite","People, perhaps from Gizon","Hashem, whose sons were among David's mighty men, came from Gizoh, a place in Judah's hill country otherwise unknown. In 2 Samuel 23:32 the same family is listed as Jashen.","group",1]],"v":[10707]},"H1452":{"l":"גְּדֵרָתִי","x":"Gᵉdêrâthîy","d":"a Gederathite, or inhabitant of Gederah","p":"ghed-ay-raw-thee'","t":"gederathi","g":"Gederathite","fb":[["gederathite","Gederathite","Gederah","Josabad was one, a Benjaminite warrior who joined David at Ziklag while Saul was still hunting him.","place",1]],"v":[10724]},"H1437":{"l":"גִּדַּלְתִּי","x":"Giddaltîy","d":"Giddalti, an Israelite","p":"ghid-dal'-tee","t":"giddalti","g":"Giddalti","fb":[["giddalti","Giddalti","Levite living at the time of Divided Monarchy","One of Heman's sons, and Heman was a Levite musician in David's court. Giddalti led one of the twenty-four divisions of temple musicians.","person",2]],"v":[11050,11075]},"H1451":{"l":"גְּדֵרִי","x":"Gᵉdêrîy","d":"a Gederite, or inhabitant of Geder","p":"ghed-ay-ree'","t":"gederi","g":"Gederite","fb":[["gederite","Gederite","Gederah","Baal-hanan, who looked after David's olive and sycamore trees in the lowlands, is called this because he came from Geder or Gederah.","place",1]],"v":[11137]},"H1485":{"l":"גּוּר־בַּעַל","x":"Gûwr-Baʻal","d":"Gur-Baal, a place in Arabia","p":"goor-bah'-al","t":"gur-baal","g":"Gur","fb":[["gur-baal","Gur-baal","","God helped King Uzziah beat the people of Gur-baal, along with the Philistines and the Meunites. The name means sojourn of Baal, so it was probably an Arabian settlement where Baal was worshipped, and nobody knows where.","place",1]],"v":[11739,11739]},"H1489":{"l":"גִּזְבָּר","x":"gizbâr","d":"treasurer","p":"ghiz-bawr'","t":"gizbar","g":"treasurer","fb":[],"v":[12024]},"H1402":{"l":"גִּבָּר","x":"Gibbâr","d":"Gibbar, an Israelite","p":"ghib-bawr'","t":"gibbar","g":"of Gibbar","fb":[["gibbar","Gibbar","Gibeon","The family came back from Babylon with Zerubbabel, ninety-five of them. Nehemiah 7:25 gives the name as Gibeon.","place",1]],"v":[12047]},"H1435":{"l":"גִּדֵּל","x":"Giddêl","d":"Giddel, the name of one of the Nethinim, also of one of 'Solomon's servants'","p":"ghid-dale'","t":"giddel","g":"of Giddel","fb":[["giddel","Giddel","Man living at the time of Exile and Return","Head of a family of temple servants, the Nethinim, in the lists of exiles coming home.","person",2],["giddel-2","Giddel","Man living at the time of Exile and Return","Head of a family among the temple servants, and separately among Solomon's servants, both counted in the return lists.","person",2]],"v":[12074,12083,12469,12478]},"H1459":{"l":"גַּו","x":"gav","d":"the middle","p":"gav","t":"gav","g":"the midst","fb":[],"v":[12125,12141,12153,21812,21817,21821,21827,21829,21830,21831,21832,21846,21947]},"H1400":{"l":"גְּבַר","x":"gᵉbar","d":null,"p":"gheb-ar'","t":"gebar","g":"men","fb":[],"v":[12131,12138,12144,12159,21782,21814,21818,21818,21819,21826,21827,21828,21829,21830,21831,21833,21884,21909,21915,21919,21928]},"H1490":{"l":"גִּזְבָּר","x":"gizbâr","d":null,"p":"ghiz-bawr'","t":"gizbar","g":"the","fb":[],"v":[12194]},"H1479":{"l":"גּוּף","x":"gûwph","d":"properly, to hollow or arch, i.e. (figuratively) close; to shut","p":"goof","t":"guph","g":"let them shut","fb":[],"v":[12423]},"H1487":{"l":"גּוּשׁ","x":"gûwsh","d":"a mass of earth","p":"goosh","t":"gush","g":"clod[s]","fb":[],"v":[13012]},"H1465":{"l":"גֵּוָה","x":"gêvâh","d":"the back, i.e. (by extension) the person","p":"gay-vaw'","t":"gevah","g":"back","fb":[],"v":[13350]